kosha clay-mineral

  -- aluminosilicate minerals with layered sheet structure.
  -- general formula: Al2Si2O5(OH)4 (kaolinite) and related structures.
  -- sheet structure: alternating SiO4 and AlO6 layers — explains plasticity.
  -- when wet: water enters between layers → clay becomes plastic (deformable).
  -- when dry: layers bind → clay hardens. fired at high temp → ceramic.
  -- kaolinite: porcelain, fine china. montmorillonite: drilling mud, cat litter.
  -- ion exchange capacity: clay holds and releases nutrient ions in soil.
  -- the plasticity of clay is mithuna at the mineral level — water and mineral
  -- together produce a third thing: something that can be shaped.

